WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:04.980
As the titular character of the drama series,
The Good Doctor, Dr. Shaun Murphy has faced

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.850
great adversity and made great triumphs.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:12.330
These are the highest of the highs and the
lowest of the lows for Shaun and those closest

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.540
to him.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:17.930
More than a year ahead of the COVID-19 pandemic,
The Good Doctor forced its doctors to deal

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:22.760
with a quick-spreading pathogen in the Season
2 fall finale episode "Quarantine."

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:28.500
The installment found St. Bonaventure's ER
on lockdown as a virus laid siege to the hospital.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.870
The drama takes place as things are already
ramping up amid holiday madness, and the pressure

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:36.700
is already heightened for Shaun, who finds
the sensory assault of Christmas lights and

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.360
holiday chaos chipping away at his composure.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.290
To make matters worse, hospital visitors begin
freaking out, emergency surgeries are needed,

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:48.489
Park's son has a severe asthma attack, and
some of the doctors are among those taking

00:00:48.489 --> 00:00:49.489
ill.

00:00:49.489 --> 00:00:54.250
Amid all of the frenzy, Shaun begins to hyperfocus
on a buzzing overhead light that continues

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:59.410
to break his concentration – a sign that
he is beginning to experience sensory overload.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:00.649
"The light is buzzing."

00:01:00.649 --> 00:01:02.050
"I don't hear anything."

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:04.330
"It's loud and very distracting.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.850
It needs to be fixed."

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:10.759
Things reach a fever pitch when Lim collapses
while walking Morgan through surgery as Park

00:01:10.759 --> 00:01:13.080
screams for someone to help his son.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.259
Shaun finally hits his breaking point, covering
his ears and curling up in a fetal position

00:01:17.259 --> 00:01:21.950
right in the middle of the emergency room
walkway as alarmed staff and patients look

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:22.950
on.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:26.259
Although it's a scary moment for Shaun and
the nursing staff, Morgan's quick thinking

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:30.450
saves the day when she realizes that getting
him to focus on the surgery is just the thing

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.610
to help him calm down.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:37.400
As a neurologically atypical individual, Shaun
sometimes struggles to communicate information

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.479
with the same ease as his neurotypical colleagues.

00:01:40.479 --> 00:01:44.630
That's alright, however, because Shaun's other
workplace gifts far exceed the communication

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:46.990
challenges he encounters from time to time.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:51.500
When Dr. Lim assigns Shaun his first surgery
in "First Case, Second Base," Shaun feels

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:56.060
confident even though his number one detractor,
Dr. Andrews, has doubts about whether Murphy

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:57.259
is up to the challenge.

00:01:57.259 --> 00:02:00.850
Although the surgery starts auspiciously,
Shaun suddenly walks out of the operating

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:02.850
room halfway through the surgery.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.009
"Can't do this!"

00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:08.020
"What can't you do?"

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.020
"No!

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.020
No!

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.020
No!"

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:14.239
Shaun then proceeds to pace the hallway while
struggling to articulate what he's thinking

00:02:14.239 --> 00:02:17.520
as a baffled Park, Andrews, and Lim look on.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:20.879
Just as Andrews and Lim are concluding Shaun
is suffering a meltdown that demonstrates

00:02:20.879 --> 00:02:25.630
how unfit he is for the job, a light bulb
goes off over Park's head as he realizes Shaun

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.530
is trying to tell them something.

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:31.160
After calming down, Shaun explains that the
patient, who would have been left with a feeding

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:35.520
tube as a result of the planned surgery, could
receive a more advanced operation – but

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.030
it would mean Shaun has to forfeit his case.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.879
The moment demonstrates how capable Shaun
is of synergy with his colleagues, his ability

00:02:41.879 --> 00:02:46.690
to overcome his own challenges, and his willingness
to put patients first.

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:50.630
From the moment Lea knocked on Shaun's apartment
door, it was clear they had chemistry.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:55.110
Still, the path to true love isn't always
easy, and both Shaun and Lea had a lot of

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:58.580
growing up to do before they were ready to
start a relationship.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:02.190
Things between the pair get rocky after Carly
breaks things off with Shaun, encouraging

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.420
him to tell Lea how he feels about her.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:08.900
In the Season 3 episode "Autopsy," Shaun follows
Carly's advice and confesses his feelings

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:09.900
for Lea.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:14.170
She is quick to reciprocate them but tearfully
says they can't be together, remaining silent

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:16.780
when he asks if it's because of his autism.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:21.299
Shaun spends the next few episodes in a dark
hole and lashes out at everyone around him

00:03:21.299 --> 00:03:22.299
in anger.

00:03:22.299 --> 00:03:26.250
Eventually, he decides to vandalize Lea's
car in the hope that it will make him feel

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:27.250
better.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:31.120
However, he can't bring himself to do it,
and instead delivers a brutal takedown, telling

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:35.610
Lea she doesn't respect him, no one likes
her, and she deserves to end up alone.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:39.090
"You acted like you cared about me.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:42.580
But you don't even respect me."

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:47.000
The interaction is distressing and cruel,
even if Lea badly needs a wake-up call to

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.120
confront her ableism and selfishness.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:54.670
One of the things that made the early difficulties
between Shaun and Lea so painful is that Lea

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:56.610
wasn't just rejecting him outright.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:04:00.510
She really does love him but genuinely worries
that a relationship between two high-maintenance

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.430
people would be far too difficult.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:06.860
However, as she takes time to think things
over, her feelings for Shaun only continue

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:11.250
to grow, and she is finally forced to face
them when she fears she might lose him for

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.250
good.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:16.079
The revelation comes in Season 3's penultimate
episode, "Hurt," which puts Shaun on the rescue

00:04:16.079 --> 00:04:20.370
team in the aftermath of an earthquake that
leaves some of St. Bonaventure's people – including

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:22.320
Lea – trapped in a brewery.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:26.540
Shaun sets out to rescue her but ends up helping
a woman named Vera instead.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:30.389
While trapped and awaiting rescue, Shaun pours
his heart out to Vera without realizing that

00:04:30.389 --> 00:04:33.070
Lea can hear him from a walkie-talkie.

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:37.270
Before he can bring her to safety, an aftershock
traps them both, flooding the sub-basement

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:40.300
as a horrified Lea listens in over the radio.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:43.580
As Lea fears for his safety, Shaun pours out
his heart to Vera.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:47.830
"Lea makes me more."

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:51.539
After Shaun's confession, an aftershock then
hits, flooding the basement and Shaun and

00:04:51.539 --> 00:04:52.910
Vera are trapped in.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:57.050
With their lives at stake, Vera convinces
Shaun to move on from Lea if they make it

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:58.050
out alive.

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:02.160
When he finally emerges from the building,
a waiting Lea greets him with a kiss, telling

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:06.690
him that he makes her feel the same way, having
finally realized how much better their lives

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.320
are together.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:12.260
It's established early in The Good Doctor
that Shaun's parents failed him badly.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:15.940
Shaun's alcoholic father was horribly abusive
to Shaun and his brother Steve.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.820
He berated Shaun for his autism.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.600
Eventually, he drove Shaun and his brother,
Steve, to run away from home, which leads

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.630
to Steve's accidental death.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:27.850
With such a tragic backstory, it's little
wonder Shaun is hesitant to go see his estranged

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:30.520
father when he learns he has a terminal illness.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:34.790
Although his father, Ethan Murphy, initially
apologizes to Shaun, he does so by playing

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:40.160
the victim, blaming his actions on his inability
to help his autistic son in "Friends and Family."

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:44.440
His words are triggering, causing Shaun to
unleash his anger, telling his father he's

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.670
a bad person.

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:54.580
"You killed my rabbit, and you killed my brother."

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:58.460
After sleeping on his anger, Shaun returns
to forgive his father, but Ethan responds

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:03.440
with more abuse, telling Shaun that he is
weak and it's his fault his brother died.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:08.090
It's a dark moment in Shaun's life that reminds
Shaun the Murphys were never his family — except

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:09.949
by blood.

00:06:09.949 --> 00:06:14.530
Shawn first meets Dr. Glassman after he and
Steve run away in search of a doctor for Shaun's

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:15.530
rabbit.

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:19.760
While Glassman can't save their pet, he gives
them his phone number in case they need anything,

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:22.440
which leads to Shaun to call him after Steve's
accident.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:26.510
Although Shaun is eventually placed in foster
care, he remains in touch with Glassman, who

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:30.580
serves as a surrogate father and helps him
get hired at St. Bonaventure after medical

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:31.580
school.

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:35.530
Through the ensuing years, their relationship
faces various trials and strains, but they

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:37.199
remain close despite everything.

00:06:37.199 --> 00:06:41.050
On Shaun's wedding day, Glassman gives Shaun
two rings passed down through his family that

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:43.190
he had intended to give his late daughter.

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:47.150
As Glassman attempts to tie Shaun's bowtie
for him, Shaun shares a touching sentiment

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:51.460
that highlights the importance each man has
in the other's life, even calling Glassman

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:52.460
his father.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:54.360
"I love you, Dr. Glassman."

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:58.599
Although Shaun faces many challenges building
relationships at St. Bonaventure, he forms

00:06:58.599 --> 00:07:01.300
a strong workplace friendship with Audrey
Lim.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:05.889
However, their relationship sours after Shaun's
split-second surgical decision leaves Lim

00:07:05.889 --> 00:07:07.440
partially paralyzed.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:11.490
The trouble arises when Dr. Lim and another
doctor are attacked during Shaun's wedding

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:16.009
at the end of Season 5, forcing Shaun and
Glassman to perform emergency surgery with

00:07:16.009 --> 00:07:20.349
the hospital still under lockdown in the Season
6 opener "Afterparty."

00:07:20.349 --> 00:07:24.539
While operating on Lim, Shaun goes against
Glassman's order, performing a slightly riskier

00:07:24.539 --> 00:07:27.879
procedure that saves her but causes her paralysis.

00:07:27.879 --> 00:07:31.879
As she struggles to accept her new reality,
Lim targets her anger on Shaun, believing

00:07:31.879 --> 00:07:36.570
his recklessness cost her the ability to walk
– a position that's unfortunately reinforced

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:39.129
by Glassman's own feelings about Shaun's decision.

00:07:39.129 --> 00:07:43.139
When Shaun doesn't seem to understand how
resentful Lim is, she brutally spells it out

00:07:43.139 --> 00:07:47.600
for him, telling Dr. Murphy that she no longer
wants to be friends in "A Big Sign."

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:48.600
"But that's all.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:54.900
I don't want you to ask me about my personal
live, and I don't want to hear about yours."

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:59.229
Fortunately for all involved, Shaun is nothing
if not persistent, and he continues to work

00:07:59.229 --> 00:08:03.110
on ways to get her mobility back despite Lim's
anger.

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:07.229
While Lim continues to harbor resentment toward
Shaun, she eventually begins to embrace her

00:08:07.229 --> 00:08:11.979
new way of living with help from Danni, who
underwent a leg amputation years prior.

00:08:11.979 --> 00:08:15.349
Despite the strain on their relationship,
Shaun's commitment to repairing Lim's nerve

00:08:15.349 --> 00:08:19.110
damage pays off when he finds a way to get
her walking again.

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:22.050
However, Shaun has to make things right with
Lim first.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:26.110
In the episode "Sorry, Not Sorry," he tells
her he does not owe her an apology, as he

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:29.909
did save her life, but admits he is sorry
the decision caused her harm.

00:08:29.909 --> 00:08:33.560
He further opens up, telling Lim he misses
their personal relationship.

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:38.469
"I have missed your friendship.

00:08:38.469 --> 00:08:42.659
I have missed you."

00:08:42.659 --> 00:08:46.660
Lim reveals she's working through her anger,
but she's finally in a good place and misses

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:48.350
Shaun's friendship, too.

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:52.300
It's good to see Lim and Shaun makeup, but
more importantly, the moment shows Shaun's

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:53.980
growth as a surgeon.

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:57.800
Shaun's revelation that he isn't remorseful
or guilty while still expressing empathy for

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:02.100
Lim shows his humanity without compromising
his confidence in his ability to make the

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:05.890
hard calls he'll need to keep making going
forward.

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:10.240
Shaun and his colleagues find themselves in
the tug-of-war between quality care and financial

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:14.330
constraints when the St. Bonaventure is bought
by the overbearing Salen.

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:18.390
While she saves the hospital from financial
ruin, Salen shifts everything to a heavily

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:22.510
profit-driven system, and begins weighing
money over human lives.

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:25.720
At first, Shaun weathers the changes surprisingly
well.

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:30.220
While he tends to resist change, he can understand
the logic behind many of Salen's decisions.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:34.900
However, when Salen's corner-cutting with
expired medications costs a baby her life,

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:38.080
Shaun's rage boils over in the episode, "Expired."

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:42.350
Triggered by the recent loss of his own infant,
he makes his way to the hospital pharmacy,

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:47.380
where he smashes bottles of expired medications
and lashes out at everyone around.

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:51.370
Feeling he can't trust anyone, blaming Glassman
for the baby's death and telling Lea that

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:52.710
he can't marry her.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:54.769
"You lied to me.

00:09:54.769 --> 00:09:58.920
I can't trust you, and I can't marry you."

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:03.209
While it's a dark moment that leaves a serious
rift in Shaun's relationship with Lea, the

00:10:03.209 --> 00:10:08.560
meltdown marks a turning point that leads
to the staff's active rebellion against Salen.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:12.310
One of the more heartbreaking storylines in
The Good Doctor is Shaun and Lea's painful

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:13.790
journey to parenthood.

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:17.600
As Lea's pregnancy progresses, they learn
they're having a baby girl and get excited

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:19.220
about their new family member.

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:23.779
However, their happiness falls apart when
Lea experiences a brutal late pregnancy loss

00:10:23.779 --> 00:10:25.410
in "Dr. Ted."

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:29.250
Over time, the couple begins to move on past
their grief, eventually getting married and

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:32.779
looking forward to starting a family once
they get the medical okay.

00:10:32.779 --> 00:10:38.020
However, Shaun and Lea are met with even more
bad news when they learn Lea has Asherman's

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:42.050
syndrome, a condition that will likely affect
Lea's fertility and ability to carry the baby

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:44.310
to term in "Boys Don't Cry."

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:48.010
Although they want to be parents, the pair
is understandably terrified when Lea gets

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:52.440
pregnant again in "Broken or Not," and their
fears are confirmed when they learn her uterus

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:55.750
is thinning and has a high probability of
rupturing.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:11:00.329
Shaun devises a surgical plan to increase
their odds, but while recovering in the hospital,

00:11:00.329 --> 00:11:03.330
Lea experiences a bleed from her scar tissue.

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:07.720
In "Quiet and Loud," Glassman tells Shaun
that Lea and the baby will survive only because

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:11.389
they were already in the hospital for Shaun's
procedure.

00:11:11.389 --> 00:11:15.639
Among the many difficult figures Shaun encounters
while working at St. Bonaventure, few are

00:11:15.639 --> 00:11:20.850
more divisive than Dr. Jackson Han, played
by Daniel Dae Kim, whose arrogance as a surgeon

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:23.010
is unrivaled among the staff.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:27.830
After Marcus Andrews ascends to hospital president,
his position is filled by Dr. Han, who finds

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:32.830
Shaun's interactions with other staffers and
patients inappropriate for a position in surgery.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:37.060
After Shaun upsets a mother with an inconvenient
truth about her infant, Han confronts him

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:40.880
only to be dumbfounded at Shaun's lack of
social awareness about his own interaction

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:43.269
with the young resident in "Risk and Reward."

00:11:43.269 --> 00:11:48.329
Despite Shaun's colleagues' insistence that
he is working on social cues, Han feels Murphy

00:11:48.329 --> 00:11:50.250
isn't fit for the role of surgeon.

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:55.380
After telling Shaun he is a remarkable diagnostician,
Han moves him into the pathology department,

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:57.970
believing it's a better fit for Shaun's social
skills.

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:02.040
For Shaun, who has dreamed of becoming a surgeon
since his youth, the move is a bitter pill

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:03.100
to swallow.

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:07.630
In "Breakdown," Shaun is brought in to consult
on a later surgery at Melendez's request.

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:11.870
He confronts Han about getting his job back
but ends up having a meltdown and that gets

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:12.870
him fired.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.589
"I am a surgeon!

00:12:14.589 --> 00:12:18.330
I am a surgeon!"

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:24.330
Han's handling of the Shaun situation widens
the rift between himself and Andrews, who

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:28.950
ends up firing Han and getting Shaun his old
job back in "Trampoline."

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:33.190
With all Shaun and Lea go through together,
it's nice to see them finally get their happy

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:34.190
ending.

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:38.250
However, because it's The Good Doctor, even
their wedding turns out to be a tricky affair.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:42.440
After struggling to heal from their tragic
pregnancy loss, the episode "Vamos" sees Shaun

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:45.990
and Lea get engaged while on a medical mission
in Guatemala.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:50.200
By the time of their engagement party, everyone
is looking forward to the upcoming nuptials,

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:54.510
but the stress of wedding planning already
has Lea struggling in "New Beginnings."

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:58.990
If that wasn't enough pressure, they agree
to be part of a streaming reality series culminating

00:12:58.990 --> 00:13:00.300
in an onscreen wedding.

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:04.480
However, when the big day comes, they hate
everything about it and decide to cancel their

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:06.760
wedding moments before showtime.

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:10.290
Just when it starts to seem like they'll never
tie the knot, Shaun and Lea decide to get

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:12.250
hitched in a courthouse wedding.

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:16.270
Before they can, Dr. Glassman and Jordan throw
together a surprise rooftop wedding with all

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:17.699
of their friends present.

00:13:17.699 --> 00:13:21.760
It's a perfect moment for an unconventional
couple, even if their fairy tale ending is

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:24.019
cut short when the hospital goes on lockdown.

